\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Payne County has come in under 90% of normal in October to November 39 times in 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 182% of normal in April to May but just 35% in January to February. So far in 2026, February to March sat at 28% and June to July at 133%. A preliminary estimate for grid 19333 puts August to September 2026 at 59.7, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
